/*
================================================================================
 align_project_baselines.dxl

 PURPOSE
   Compares two DOORS projects that are meant to be "the same project" (e.g.
   two copies / branches / environments of one project tree) and aligns their
   Baseline Set Definitions (BSDs) so that:

     1. Both projects have the same set of named Baseline Set Definitions,
        WHEREVER in the folder tree they live (BSDs can be defined on the
        project root or on any subfolder - the script walks the whole tree
        recursively, not just the top folder).
     2. Each BSD contains the same member modules in both projects.
     3. Each BSD has the same set of captured Baseline Set versions
        (versionID) in both projects.

   A DXL dialog lets the admin manually MAP a Baseline Set Definition in
   Project A to the corresponding (but possibly differently-named) Baseline
   Set Definition in Project B, instead of relying on the two names matching
   exactly. BSDs that share both the same relative subfolder path AND the
   same name are pre-matched automatically as a starting point; the admin
   can remove or change any of those, and add mappings for anything named
   differently. Anything left unmapped when "Run Alignment" is clicked is
   treated as genuinely new and is created fresh on the other side, in the
   matching subfolder (if that subfolder doesn't exist on the other side,
   the script warns and skips rather than guessing / creating folders).

 A NOTE ON ARRAYS IN DXL (IMPORTANT - READ THIS)
   Unlike arrays in many modern languages, plain DXL arrays are FIXED SIZE:
   you must declare their maximum capacity up front (e.g. "string x[500]"),
   and you cannot grow them past that by simply assigning to a new index.
   There is no built-in "push"/"append" for plain arrays.

   Because of this, every list this script builds (Baseline Set Definition
   names, member module paths, captured version IDs, GUI list contents,
   etc.) is represented as a PAIR of things:
     - a fixed-size array declared with a generous maximum capacity, and
     - a plain "int ...Count" variable that tracks how many of those slots
       are actually in use right now.
   "Appending" to one of these lists means: check count < capacity, write
   into arr[count], then increment count. Every place that does this also
   logs a warning (via capacityWarning()) if the capacity would be
   exceeded, so the script fails gracefully and visibly instead of silently
   dropping data or erroring out deep inside DOORS.

   The capacity numbers are controlled from TWO places that must be kept in
   sync if you ever need to raise them:
     1. The MAX_BSDS / MAX_MEMBERS / MAX_VERSIONS int variables just below
        (used in all the "< MAX_..." bounds checks).
     2. The literal number in every "string someArray[500]" (etc.)
        declaration that is sized off one of those constants. DXL array
        sizes must be given directly, so the literal has to be typed out
        again at each declaration - each such line has a comment noting
        which constant it must match.
   If you have more than ~500 Baseline Set Definitions total, more than
   ~5000 modules in a single Baseline Set Definition, or more than ~500
   captured versions under one BSD, raise both the constant and every
   matching literal before running.

   The one exception is the "Skip" type used inside createBaselineSetCapture()
   below - Skip is a genuinely dynamic, growable DOORS container (confirmed
   from a working community DXL example), unlike plain arrays, so it does
   not need a pre-declared capacity.

 DOORS DATA MODEL USED (DXL 9.6/9.7 reference manual + community examples)
   Folder                  - a Project is just a top-level Folder; Folders
                             can nest arbitrarily deep.
   Item                    - generic handle for any folder child (Folder,
                             Project, Formal/Link/Descriptive module, etc.);
                             type(item) tells you which.
   BaselineSetDefinition   - a named "recipe": which modules belong to a
                             set. Can be defined on the project root or on
                             ANY folder within the project.
   BaselineSet             - one captured/versioned snapshot of a BSD
                             (has a versionID, e.g. "1.0").
   ModName_                - a lightweight reference to a module (by path),
                             used with module()/addModule() so you do not
                             have to open the module read/write.
   ModuleVersion           - the frozen copy of a module inside a
                             BaselineSet (has versionString/fullName).

 !!! IMPORTANT SAFETY NOTES - READ BEFORE RUNNING !!!
   - Baselines and Baseline Set captures are effectively permanent in DOORS;
     ordinary users/admins cannot cleanly "undo" a capture. ALWAYS test this
     against copies of the two projects (or a sandbox) before running it
     against production projects.
   - This script CANNOT recreate the historical content of a baseline that
     was captured in the "ahead" project days/weeks/months ago. If a
     Baseline Set version is missing from the "behind" project, the only
     thing DXL can do is capture a NEW Baseline Set today, using whatever
     content the behind project's modules currently contain. That new
     capture is tagged with the same version label for structural
     consistency, but it is NOT a byte-for-byte historical replica.
     Because of this, creating missing captures is opt-in (see
     CREATE_MISSING_BASELINE_SETS below) and off by default.
   - Adding a module to a Baseline Set Definition's membership only works if
     that module already exists (at the matching relative path) in the
     target project. The script cannot create modules that don't exist yet;
     it will log those as warnings for a human to resolve.
   - When a BSD is unmapped and only exists on one side, this script only
     creates the matching BSD if the SAME relative subfolder path already
     exists on the other side. It never creates folders on its own.
   - The GUI calls below (create/label/list/field/apply/ok/close/get/insert/
     delete/set/show/hide/destroy) and the recursive folder-walk pattern are
     assembled from several independently confirmed working DXL examples
     (DOORS DXL forum, jazz.net archive, community blogs). The Baseline/
     BaselineSet/BaselineSetDefinition calls are likewise reconstructed from
     the DXL reference manual's table of contents plus working community
     examples, not a single verbatim source I could fully re-verify page by
     page. Test on a sandbox project first, and expect to nudge minor syntax
     if your exact 9.7.2 build differs.

 CONFIGURE THE SECTION BELOW, THEN RUN FROM THE DXL EDITOR (Tools > Edit DXL)
================================================================================
*/

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONFIGURATION - edit these before running
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

string PROJ_A_PATH = "/Project A"     // full DOORS path to first project
string PROJ_B_PATH = "/Project B"     // full DOORS path to second project

// Dry run by default. Set true only after you have reviewed the report
// and are running against a test copy of the projects.
bool APPLY_CHANGES = false

// Even with APPLY_CHANGES = true, missing *captured* Baseline Set versions
// are only created if this is also true (see the safety note above).
bool CREATE_MISSING_BASELINE_SETS = false

// Optional: also write the log to a text file. Leave "" to log to the
// DXL output window only.
string LOG_FILE_PATH = ""

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// ARRAY CAPACITY LIMITS - see "A NOTE ON ARRAYS IN DXL" above.
// These are used in bounds checks; every fixed-size array declaration
// elsewhere in the file has a comment saying which of these it must
// match. Raise both together if you hit a capacity warning.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

int MAX_BSDS     = 500   // combined max Baseline Set Definitions per project
int MAX_MEMBERS  = 5000  // max member modules in a single Baseline Set Definition
int MAX_VERSIONS = 500   // max captured Baseline Set versions under one BSD

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOGGING
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

bool useLogFile_ = (LOG_FILE_PATH != "")
Stream logStream_

void openLog()
{
    if (useLogFile_)
        logStream_ = write(LOG_FILE_PATH)
}

// Central logging function - everything the script reports goes through
// here so it always goes to both the DXL output window and (optionally)
// the log file at the same time.
void log(string s)
{
    print s "\n"
    if (useLogFile_)
        logStream_ << s << "\n"
}

void closeLog()
{
    if (useLogFile_)
        close(logStream_)
}

// Standard warning printed whenever a fixed-size array would have been
// asked to hold more items than its declared capacity. See the note at
// the top of the file about keeping MAX_* constants and array-size
// literals in sync.
void capacityWarning(string what, int max)
{
    log("  WARNING: \"" what "\" reached its capacity of " max
        " entries. Some items were skipped. Raise the matching MAX_* "
        "constant AND array-size literal near the top of this script, then re-run.")
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// SMALL STRING / PATH HELPERS
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

// Returns the part of "full" that comes after the "prefix" characters.
// Used to turn an absolute folder/module path into a path that is
// relative to a project's root. This works purely on individual
// characters via string indexing/concatenation, so it is not affected by
// the fixed-array-capacity issue described above.
string stripPrefix(string full, string prefix)
{
    int lenPrefix = length(prefix)
    int lenFull   = length(full)
    string result = ""

    if (lenFull <= lenPrefix)
        return result

    int i
    for i in lenPrefix:lenFull-1 do
        result = result full[i]

    return result
}

// Checks whether "val" is present among the first "count" entries of
// "arr". "count" is passed explicitly (rather than using the array's
// declared capacity) because the array itself will usually be larger
// than the number of entries actually in use - see the note on arrays
// at the top of this file.
bool arrayContains(string arr[], int count, string val)
{
    if (count == 0)
        return false

    int i
    for i in 0:count-1 do
        if (arr[i] == val)
            return true

    return false
}

// Resolves a folder given a project root path and a path relative to that
// root ("" means the project root itself).
Folder resolveFolderByRelPath(string projRootFull, string relPath)
{
    if (relPath == "")
        return folder(projRootFull)
    return folder(projRootFull relPath)
}

// Human-readable label for a (folder, name) pair, used in the GUI lists,
// e.g. "/SubSystem/Requirements :: Release Set" or
// "(project root) :: Release Set".
string formatEntry(string folderRel, string bsdName)
{
    if (folderRel == "")
        return "(project root) :: " bsdName
    return folderRel " :: " bsdName
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// GLOBAL STATE FOR THE MAPPING DIALOG
//
// Every list below is a fixed-size array plus a "...Count" variable
// giving the number of slots currently in use (see the note on arrays
// at the top of the file). The array sizes (500) must match MAX_BSDS.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

string g_dlgRootA
string g_dlgRootB

// Confirmed mappings: pair i (for i in 0..g_mapCount-1) is
// (g_mapNameA[i] in g_mapFolderA[i]) <-> (g_mapNameB[i] in g_mapFolderB[i])
string g_mapNameA[500]     // size must match MAX_BSDS
string g_mapFolderA[500]   // size must match MAX_BSDS
string g_mapNameB[500]     // size must match MAX_BSDS
string g_mapFolderB[500]   // size must match MAX_BSDS
int    g_mapCount = 0

// What is currently shown (still unmapped) on the Project A side.
// g_curA holds the display strings (what the widget shows, and what
// get(g_listA, i) returns); g_curNameA / g_curFolderA hold the real
// underlying data, always kept in lock-step with g_curA by index.
string g_curA[500]         // size must match MAX_BSDS
string g_curNameA[500]     // size must match MAX_BSDS
string g_curFolderA[500]   // size must match MAX_BSDS
int    g_curACount = 0

// Same idea, for the Project B side.
string g_curB[500]         // size must match MAX_BSDS
string g_curNameB[500]     // size must match MAX_BSDS
string g_curFolderB[500]   // size must match MAX_BSDS
int    g_curBCount = 0

DB  g_mapDlg
DBE g_listA
DBE g_listB
DBE g_listMap
DBE g_status

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// ARRAY BOOKKEEPING HELPERS FOR THE MAPPING DIALOG
//
// These operate directly on the fixed-size globals above by SHIFTING
// entries left or right in place and adjusting the relevant "...Count"
// variable - there is no array resizing or reassignment anywhere here,
// only writes to existing, already-declared slots.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

// Removes the entry at index "idx" from the Project A "still unmapped"
// list by shifting every later entry one slot to the left, then
// shrinking the count by one. (If idx is the last used slot, the shift
// loop below simply does nothing, which is exactly what we want.)
void removeFromCurA(int idx)
{
    int i
    for i in idx:g_curACount-2 do
    {
        g_curA[i] = g_curA[i+1]
        g_curNameA[i] = g_curNameA[i+1]
        g_curFolderA[i] = g_curFolderA[i+1]
    }
    g_curACount = g_curACount - 1
}

// Same as removeFromCurA, for the Project B side.
void removeFromCurB(int idx)
{
    int i
    for i in idx:g_curBCount-2 do
    {
        g_curB[i] = g_curB[i+1]
        g_curNameB[i] = g_curNameB[i+1]
        g_curFolderB[i] = g_curFolderB[i+1]
    }
    g_curBCount = g_curBCount - 1
}

// Adds one entry back to the FRONT of the Project A "still unmapped"
// list (used when the admin removes a confirmed mapping). Every existing
// entry is shifted one slot to the right first to make room at index 0.
void prependToCurA(string disp, string nm, string fld)
{
    if (g_curACount >= 500)   // must match MAX_BSDS
    {
        capacityWarning("Project A unmapped BSD list", MAX_BSDS)
        return
    }

    int i = g_curACount
    while (i > 0)
    {
        g_curA[i] = g_curA[i-1]
        g_curNameA[i] = g_curNameA[i-1]
        g_curFolderA[i] = g_curFolderA[i-1]
        i = i - 1
    }
    g_curA[0] = disp
    g_curNameA[0] = nm
    g_curFolderA[0] = fld
    g_curACount = g_curACount + 1
}

// Same as prependToCurA, for the Project B side.
void prependToCurB(string disp, string nm, string fld)
{
    if (g_curBCount >= 500)   // must match MAX_BSDS
    {
        capacityWarning("Project B unmapped BSD list", MAX_BSDS)
        return
    }

    int i = g_curBCount
    while (i > 0)
    {
        g_curB[i] = g_curB[i-1]
        g_curNameB[i] = g_curNameB[i-1]
        g_curFolderB[i] = g_curFolderB[i-1]
        i = i - 1
    }
    g_curB[0] = disp
    g_curNameB[0] = nm
    g_curFolderB[0] = fld
    g_curBCount = g_curBCount + 1
}

// Removes the confirmed mapping at index "idx" by shifting every later
// mapping one slot to the left across all four parallel arrays, then
// shrinking g_mapCount.
void removeMappingAt(int idx)
{
    int i
    for i in idx:g_mapCount-2 do
    {
        g_mapNameA[i] = g_mapNameA[i+1]
        g_mapFolderA[i] = g_mapFolderA[i+1]
        g_mapNameB[i] = g_mapNameB[i+1]
        g_mapFolderB[i] = g_mapFolderB[i+1]
    }
    g_mapCount = g_mapCount - 1
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// BASELINE / BSD HELPERS
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

// Searches the Baseline Set Definitions defined DIRECTLY on one folder
// (not its subfolders) for one named "bsdName". Returns true and sets
// outBsd if found.
bool findBSDByNameInFolder(Folder fld, string bsdName, BaselineSetDefinition &outBsd)
{
    if (null fld)
        return false

    BaselineSetDefinition b
    for b in fld do
    {
        if (name(b) == bsdName)
        {
            outBsd = b
            return true
        }
    }
    return false
}

// Resolves a BSD given a project root, a folder relative to that root
// ("" = project root), and the BSD's name. This is how we turn the
// (root, folder, name) triples stored in the mapping dialog's arrays
// back into a real, usable BaselineSetDefinition handle whenever we
// actually need to act on one.
bool findBSD(string projRootFull, string relFolderPath, string bsdName, BaselineSetDefinition &outBsd)
{
    Folder fld = resolveFolderByRelPath(projRootFull, relFolderPath)
    return findBSDByNameInFolder(fld, bsdName, outBsd)
}

// Recursively walks a folder tree, collecting every Baseline Set
// Definition found anywhere in it (the folder itself, and every
// subfolder underneath), along with the path of the folder it lives on,
// relative to the project root. "names"/"folders" are fixed-size arrays
// (capacity MAX_BSDS) supplied by the caller; "count" is passed by
// reference so it keeps accumulating correctly across every recursive
// call, since all calls share the same underlying counter.
void collectBSDsRecursive(Folder fld, string projRootFull, string names[], string folders[], int &count)
{
    string relHere = stripPrefix(fullName(fld), projRootFull)

    // Baseline Set Definitions that live directly on this folder.
    BaselineSetDefinition b
    for b in fld do
    {
        if (count < MAX_BSDS)
        {
            names[count] = name(b)
            folders[count] = relHere
            count = count + 1
        }
        else
            capacityWarning("Baseline Set Definition list", MAX_BSDS)
    }

    // Recurse into every subfolder (and nested sub-project, if any).
    Item itm
    for itm in fld do
    {
        if (type(itm) == "Folder" || type(itm) == "Project")
        {
            Folder sub = folder(fullName(itm))
            collectBSDsRecursive(sub, projRootFull, names, folders, count)
        }
    }
}

// Collects the relative (project-root-stripped) paths of every module
// that is a member of the given BSD. "relPaths" has capacity MAX_MEMBERS;
// "count" is passed by reference and updated as entries are added.
void getMemberRelativePaths(BaselineSetDefinition bsd, string projRootFull, string relPaths[], int &count)
{
    ModName_ m
    for m in bsd do
    {
        if (count < MAX_MEMBERS)
        {
            relPaths[count] = stripPrefix(fullName(m), projRootFull)
            count = count + 1
        }
        else
            capacityWarning("member module list", MAX_MEMBERS)
    }
}

// Collects the versionID of every BaselineSet captured under a BSD.
// "versions" has capacity MAX_VERSIONS; "count" is passed by reference.
void getCapturedVersions(BaselineSetDefinition bsd, string versions[], int &count)
{
    BaselineSet bs
    for bs in bsd do
    {
        if (count < MAX_VERSIONS)
        {
            versions[count] = versionID(bs)
            count = count + 1
        }
        else
            capacityWarning("captured Baseline Set version list", MAX_VERSIONS)
    }
}

// Recursively counts every captured Baseline Set anywhere in the project
// tree. Used only for the informational summary line printed in main();
// this is a plain running total (an int, not an array), so it is not
// affected by the fixed-array-capacity issue.
int countCapturedBaselineSetsRecursive(Folder fld)
{
    int total = 0

    BaselineSetDefinition b
    for b in fld do
    {
        BaselineSet bs
        for bs in b do
            total++
    }

    Item itm
    for itm in fld do
        if (type(itm) == "Folder" || type(itm) == "Project")
            total = total + countCapturedBaselineSetsRecursive(folder(fullName(itm)))

    return total
}

// Adds one module (identified by its path relative to the target
// project's root) to a BaselineSetDefinition's membership. Looks the
// module up by path via module() rather than opening it, so this does
// not require a read/write lock on the module itself.
void addMissingModule(string projRootFull, BaselineSetDefinition bsd, string relPath)
{
    string fullPath = projRootFull relPath
    ModName_ m = module(fullPath)

    if (null m)
    {
        log("    WARNING: no module found at \"" fullPath "\" - cannot add. "
            "The module may not exist there yet; resolve manually.")
        return
    }

    string err = addModule(m, bsd)
    if (!null err)
        log("    ERROR adding module \"" fullPath "\" to BSD \"" name(bsd) "\": " err)
    else
        log("    Added module \"" fullPath "\" to BSD \"" name(bsd) "\"")
}

// Creates a missing BaselineSetDefinition on the given target folder,
// copying the description from the source project's BSD but keeping the
// name the admin asked for (may differ from the source BSD's name).
bool createMissingBSD(Folder targetFolder, string bsdName, string bsdDesc, BaselineSetDefinition &outBsd)
{
    if (null targetFolder)
    {
        log("  ERROR: destination folder does not exist - cannot create Baseline Set Definition \""
            bsdName "\" there.")
        return false
    }

    string err = create(targetFolder, bsdName, bsdDesc, outBsd)
    if (!null err)
    {
        log("  ERROR creating Baseline Set Definition \"" bsdName "\": " err)
        return false
    }
    log("  Created Baseline Set Definition \"" bsdName "\" on " fullName(targetFolder))
    return true
}

// Captures a brand-new Baseline Set for the given BSD, using whatever
// modules currently sit in it, tagged with the supplied version label.
// See the safety note at the top of this file: this is NOT a historical
// replica, it's a fresh capture taken right now.
//
// NOTE: "Skip" here is a genuinely dynamic DOORS container (confirmed
// from a working community DXL example) - unlike the plain string/bool
// arrays used everywhere else in this file, it does not need a
// pre-declared capacity, so put() can just keep growing it.
bool createBaselineSetCapture(BaselineSetDefinition bsd, string versionLabel, string desc)
{
    string err = lock(bsd)
    if (!null err)
    {
        log("    ERROR locking BSD \"" name(bsd) "\" before capture: " err)
        return false
    }

    Skip modList = create
    int idx = 0
    ModName_ m
    for m in bsd do
    {
        put(modList, idx, m)
        idx++
    }

    BaselineSet newBs
    string createErr = create(bsd, true, versionLabel, desc, newBs)
    unlock(bsd)

    if (!null createErr)
    {
        log("    ERROR creating Baseline Set \"" versionLabel "\" for BSD \"" name(bsd) "\": " createErr)
        return false
    }

    string addErr = addBaselines(modList, newBs)
    if (!null addErr)
        log("    WARNING while capturing modules into \"" versionLabel "\": " addErr)

    close(newBs)
    log("    Captured new Baseline Set \"" versionLabel "\" for BSD \"" name(bsd) "\" "
        "(content reflects the target project's state right now, not the original baseline date).")
    return true
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// ALIGNMENT ENGINE
// (operates on one already-resolved pair of BSDs at a time; direction
//  - which side is "ahead"/"behind" - is decided per pair by comparing
//  how many Baseline Sets each side has already captured)
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

// Brings "targetBsd" (in targetRoot's project) up to date with
// "refBsd" (in refRoot's project): adds any member modules refBsd has
// that targetBsd doesn't, and (optionally) captures any Baseline Set
// versions refBsd has that targetBsd is missing.
void alignOneDirection(BaselineSetDefinition refBsd, string refRoot,
                        BaselineSetDefinition targetBsd, string targetRoot)
{
    // ---- step 1: compare member-module lists ----

    string refMembers[5000]        // size must match MAX_MEMBERS
    int refMembersCount = 0
    getMemberRelativePaths(refBsd, refRoot, refMembers, refMembersCount)

    string targetMembers[5000]     // size must match MAX_MEMBERS
    int targetMembersCount = 0
    getMemberRelativePaths(targetBsd, targetRoot, targetMembers, targetMembersCount)

    string missingMembers[5000]    // size must match MAX_MEMBERS
    int missingMembersCount = 0
    int i
    if (refMembersCount > 0)
    {
        for i in 0:refMembersCount-1 do
        {
            if (!arrayContains(targetMembers, targetMembersCount, refMembers[i]))
            {
                if (missingMembersCount < MAX_MEMBERS)
                {
                    missingMembers[missingMembersCount] = refMembers[i]
                    missingMembersCount = missingMembersCount + 1
                }
                else
                    capacityWarning("missing-member list", MAX_MEMBERS)
            }
        }
    }

    if (missingMembersCount > 0)
    {
        log("  " missingMembersCount " module(s) missing from target BSD membership:")
        for i in 0:missingMembersCount-1 do
            log("    - " missingMembers[i])

        if (APPLY_CHANGES)
        {
            string lockErr = lock(targetBsd)
            if (null lockErr)
            {
                for i in 0:missingMembersCount-1 do
                    addMissingModule(targetRoot, targetBsd, missingMembers[i])
                save(targetBsd)
                unlock(targetBsd)
            }
            else
                log("  ERROR locking target BSD for membership update: " lockErr)
        }
        else
            log("  (dry run - set APPLY_CHANGES = true to add these)")
    }
    else
        log("  Module membership already aligned.")

    // ---- step 2: compare captured Baseline Set version lists ----

    string refVersions[500]        // size must match MAX_VERSIONS
    int refVersionsCount = 0
    getCapturedVersions(refBsd, refVersions, refVersionsCount)

    string targetVersions[500]     // size must match MAX_VERSIONS
    int targetVersionsCount = 0
    getCapturedVersions(targetBsd, targetVersions, targetVersionsCount)

    string missingVersions[500]    // size must match MAX_VERSIONS
    int missingVersionsCount = 0
    if (refVersionsCount > 0)
    {
        for i in 0:refVersionsCount-1 do
        {
            if (!arrayContains(targetVersions, targetVersionsCount, refVersions[i]))
            {
                if (missingVersionsCount < MAX_VERSIONS)
                {
                    missingVersions[missingVersionsCount] = refVersions[i]
                    missingVersionsCount = missingVersionsCount + 1
                }
                else
                    capacityWarning("missing-version list", MAX_VERSIONS)
            }
        }
    }

    if (missingVersionsCount > 0)
    {
        log("  " missingVersionsCount " Baseline Set version(s) captured on the reference side but not on the target side:")
        for i in 0:missingVersionsCount-1 do
            log("    - " missingVersions[i])

        if (APPLY_CHANGES && CREATE_MISSING_BASELINE_SETS)
        {
            for i in 0:missingVersionsCount-1 do
            {
                // Find the matching captured set on the reference side so
                // we can copy its description into the new capture.
                string desc = ""
                BaselineSet matchBs
                for matchBs in refBsd do
                    if (versionID(matchBs) == missingVersions[i])
                        desc = description(matchBs)

                string note = desc " [structurally synced by align_project_baselines.dxl - "
                               "content captured at sync time, not the original baseline date]"
                createBaselineSetCapture(targetBsd, missingVersions[i], note)
            }
        }
        else
            log("    (not created - set APPLY_CHANGES = true AND CREATE_MISSING_BASELINE_SETS = true to capture these now)")
    }
    else
        log("  Captured Baseline Set versions already aligned.")
}

// Aligns one confirmed pair of BSDs: (bsdNameA, in folder folderA of
// Project A) <-> (bsdNameB, in folder folderB of Project B). Direction is
// chosen by whichever side has captured fewer Baseline Sets so far -
// that side is treated as "behind" and gets caught up to the other.
void alignPair(string rootA, string folderA, string bsdNameA,
               string rootB, string folderB, string bsdNameB)
{
    BaselineSetDefinition bsdA
    BaselineSetDefinition bsdB
    bool foundA = findBSD(rootA, folderA, bsdNameA, bsdA)
    bool foundB = findBSD(rootB, folderB, bsdNameB, bsdB)

    if (!foundA || !foundB)
    {
        log("  ERROR: could not re-locate mapped BSD \"" bsdNameA "\" (folder \""
            (folderA == "" ? "root" : folderA) "\") <-> \"" bsdNameB "\" (folder \""
            (folderB == "" ? "root" : folderB) "\") - skipping.")
        return
    }

    // Count captured Baseline Sets on each side to decide direction.
    int countA = 0
    BaselineSet tmpBs
    for tmpBs in bsdA do
        countA++
    int countB = 0
    for tmpBs in bsdB do
        countB++

    log("")
    log("BSD pair: \"" bsdNameA "\" in " (folderA == "" ? "project root" : folderA)
        " (Project A, " countA " captured set(s)) <-> \"" bsdNameB "\" in "
        (folderB == "" ? "project root" : folderB) " (Project B, " countB " captured set(s))")

    if (countA >= countB)
        alignOneDirection(bsdA, rootA, bsdB, rootB)   // A is ahead (or tied); B catches up
    else
        alignOneDirection(bsdB, rootB, bsdA, rootA)   // B is ahead; A catches up
}

// Handles a BSD that only exists on one side: creates a same-named BSD on
// the matching subfolder on the other side, mirrors its membership, and
// (optionally) its captured Baseline Set versions.
void createFreshBSDCopy(string sourceRoot, string folderRel, string bsdName, string destRoot)
{
    log("")
    log("BSD \"" bsdName "\" (folder \"" (folderRel == "" ? "project root" : folderRel)
        "\") exists only on one side.")

    if (!APPLY_CHANGES)
    {
        log("  (dry run - set APPLY_CHANGES = true to create a matching BSD on the other side)")
        return
    }

    BaselineSetDefinition sourceBsd
    if (!findBSD(sourceRoot, folderRel, bsdName, sourceBsd))
    {
        log("  ERROR: could not re-locate source BSD - skipping.")
        return
    }

    // The new BSD must land on the SAME relative folder on the other
    // side. We do not create folders ourselves - if it isn't there, warn
    // and skip so the admin can decide what to do.
    Folder destFolder = resolveFolderByRelPath(destRoot, folderRel)
    if (null destFolder)
    {
        log("  WARNING: the corresponding folder \"" (folderRel == "" ? "(project root)" : folderRel)
            "\" does not exist on the other side, so a matching Baseline Set Definition cannot be "
            "created there. Create the folder structure first (or map this BSD manually), then re-run.")
        return
    }

    BaselineSetDefinition newBsd
    if (!createMissingBSD(destFolder, bsdName, description(sourceBsd), newBsd))
        return

    // Mirror membership.
    string sourceMembers[5000]     // size must match MAX_MEMBERS
    int sourceMembersCount = 0
    getMemberRelativePaths(sourceBsd, sourceRoot, sourceMembers, sourceMembersCount)

    if (sourceMembersCount > 0)
    {
        string lockErr = lock(newBsd)
        if (null lockErr)
        {
            int i
            for i in 0:sourceMembersCount-1 do
                addMissingModule(destRoot, newBsd, sourceMembers[i])
            save(newBsd)
            unlock(newBsd)
        }
        else
            log("  ERROR locking newly created BSD: " lockErr)
    }

    // Optionally mirror captured versions too (subject to the same
    // "this is a fresh capture, not history" caveat as elsewhere).
    if (CREATE_MISSING_BASELINE_SETS)
    {
        string versions[500]       // size must match MAX_VERSIONS
        int versionsCount = 0
        getCapturedVersions(sourceBsd, versions, versionsCount)
        if (versionsCount > 0)
        {
            int i
            for i in 0:versionsCount-1 do
            {
                string desc = ""
                BaselineSet matchBs
                for matchBs in sourceBsd do
                    if (versionID(matchBs) == versions[i])
                        desc = description(matchBs)
                string note = desc " [structurally synced by align_project_baselines.dxl]"
                createBaselineSetCapture(newBsd, versions[i], note)
            }
        }
    }
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// MAPPING DIALOG CALLBACKS
//
// DXL's dialog widgets are event-driven: show(g_mapDlg) returns
// immediately, and everything else happens inside these callback
// functions as the admin clicks buttons. That is also why all the state
// they need (g_mapNameA, g_curA, etc.) lives in globals rather than
// local variables - each callback is invoked fresh by DOORS with no
// memory of anything except what is stored globally.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

// "Map Selected Pair ->": takes whatever is currently selected in each
// unmapped list and turns it into a confirmed mapping.
void cbAddMapping(DB d)
{
    int i = get(g_listA)   // selected index in the Project A list, or -1
    int j = get(g_listB)   // selected index in the Project B list, or -1

    if (i < 0 || j < 0)
    {
        set(g_status, "Select one item in BOTH lists before mapping.")
        return
    }

    if (g_mapCount >= 500)   // must match MAX_BSDS
    {
        set(g_status, "Mapping list is full - cannot map any more pairs.")
        capacityWarning("confirmed mapping list", MAX_BSDS)
        return
    }

    string dispA = g_curA[i]
    string dispB = g_curB[j]
    string nameA = g_curNameA[i]
    string foldA = g_curFolderA[i]
    string nameB = g_curNameB[j]
    string foldB = g_curFolderB[j]

    // Record the confirmed mapping.
    g_mapNameA[g_mapCount] = nameA
    g_mapFolderA[g_mapCount] = foldA
    g_mapNameB[g_mapCount] = nameB
    g_mapFolderB[g_mapCount] = foldB
    insert(g_listMap, g_mapCount, dispA " -> " dispB)
    g_mapCount = g_mapCount + 1

    // Remove both items from the "still unmapped" lists (widget + our
    // bookkeeping arrays) so they can't accidentally be mapped again.
    delete(g_listA, i)
    delete(g_listB, j)
    removeFromCurA(i)
    removeFromCurB(j)

    set(g_status, "Mapped \"" dispA "\" -> \"" dispB "\".")
}

// "Remove Selected Mapping": undoes a confirmed mapping and puts both
// sides back into their respective "still unmapped" lists.
void cbRemoveMapping(DB d)
{
    int k = get(g_listMap)
    if (k < 0)
    {
        set(g_status, "Select a confirmed mapping to remove first.")
        return
    }

    string nameA = g_mapNameA[k]
    string foldA = g_mapFolderA[k]
    string nameB = g_mapNameB[k]
    string foldB = g_mapFolderB[k]

    string dispA = formatEntry(foldA, nameA)
    string dispB = formatEntry(foldB, nameB)

    insert(g_listA, 0, dispA)
    insert(g_listB, 0, dispB)
    prependToCurA(dispA, nameA, foldA)
    prependToCurB(dispB, nameB, foldB)

    delete(g_listMap, k)
    removeMappingAt(k)

    set(g_status, "Removed mapping for \"" dispA "\" - it is back in the unmapped lists.")
}

// "Run Alignment": closes the dialog and performs the actual work -
// aligning every confirmed pair, then creating fresh BSDs for whatever
// was left unmapped on either side.
void cbRunAlignment(DB d)
{
    hide(d)
    destroy(d)

    log("")
    log("================================================================")
    log("User confirmed BSD mapping - proceeding with alignment.")
    log("================================================================")

    int i

    log("Confirmed mappings (Project A <-> Project B):")
    if (g_mapCount > 0)
    {
        for i in 0:g_mapCount-1 do
            log("  \"" g_mapNameA[i] "\" (" (g_mapFolderA[i] == "" ? "root" : g_mapFolderA[i])
                ") <-> \"" g_mapNameB[i] "\" (" (g_mapFolderB[i] == "" ? "root" : g_mapFolderB[i]) ")")
    }
    else
        log("  (none)")

    if (g_curACount > 0)
    {
        log("BSDs left unmapped in Project A:")
        for i in 0:g_curACount-1 do
            log("  \"" g_curNameA[i] "\" (" (g_curFolderA[i] == "" ? "root" : g_curFolderA[i]) ")")
    }
    if (g_curBCount > 0)
    {
        log("BSDs left unmapped in Project B:")
        for i in 0:g_curBCount-1 do
            log("  \"" g_curNameB[i] "\" (" (g_curFolderB[i] == "" ? "root" : g_curFolderB[i]) ")")
    }

    // 1. process confirmed pairs (exists on both sides, possibly
    //    different names and/or different folders)
    if (g_mapCount > 0)
        for i in 0:g_mapCount-1 do
            alignPair(g_dlgRootA, g_mapFolderA[i], g_mapNameA[i],
                      g_dlgRootB, g_mapFolderB[i], g_mapNameB[i])

    // 2. A-only leftovers -> create fresh in B, same relative folder
    if (g_curACount > 0)
        for i in 0:g_curACount-1 do
            createFreshBSDCopy(g_dlgRootA, g_curFolderA[i], g_curNameA[i], g_dlgRootB)

    // 3. B-only leftovers -> create fresh in A, same relative folder
    if (g_curBCount > 0)
        for i in 0:g_curBCount-1 do
            createFreshBSDCopy(g_dlgRootB, g_curFolderB[i], g_curNameB[i], g_dlgRootA)

    log("")
    log("Alignment run complete.")
    closeLog()
}

// Dialog cancelled (Cancel button or the window's own close box) - do
// nothing further, just log and clean up.
void cbCancelMapping(DB d)
{
    hide(d)
    destroy(d)
    log("")
    log("User cancelled at the mapping dialog. No changes made.")
    closeLog()
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// MAPPING DIALOG BUILDER
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

void showMappingDialog(Folder projA, string rootA, Folder projB, string rootB)
{
    g_dlgRootA = rootA
    g_dlgRootB = rootB

    // ---- 1. collect every BSD in each project, anywhere in the tree ----

    string namesA[500]     // size must match MAX_BSDS
    string foldersA[500]   // size must match MAX_BSDS
    int namesACount = 0
    collectBSDsRecursive(projA, rootA, namesA, foldersA, namesACount)

    string namesB[500]     // size must match MAX_BSDS
    string foldersB[500]   // size must match MAX_BSDS
    int namesBCount = 0
    collectBSDsRecursive(projB, rootB, namesB, foldersB, namesBCount)

    // Reset all the mapping-dialog globals for this run (in case the
    // script is somehow invoked more than once in the same session).
    g_mapCount = 0
    g_curACount = 0
    g_curBCount = 0

    // ---- 2. auto-pre-match BSDs that share both folder AND name ----

    bool usedB[500]         // size must match MAX_BSDS; marks B-side
                             // entries already claimed by an auto-match
    int j
    if (namesBCount > 0)
        for j in 0:namesBCount-1 do
            usedB[j] = false

    int i
    if (namesACount > 0)
    {
        for i in 0:namesACount-1 do
        {
            int matchIdx = -1
            if (namesBCount > 0)
            {
                for j in 0:namesBCount-1 do
                    if (!usedB[j] && namesB[j] == namesA[i] && foldersB[j] == foldersA[i])
                        matchIdx = j
            }

            if (matchIdx >= 0)
            {
                // Exact folder+name match - pre-confirm this mapping.
                usedB[matchIdx] = true
                if (g_mapCount < MAX_BSDS)
                {
                    g_mapNameA[g_mapCount] = namesA[i]
                    g_mapFolderA[g_mapCount] = foldersA[i]
                    g_mapNameB[g_mapCount] = namesB[matchIdx]
                    g_mapFolderB[g_mapCount] = foldersB[matchIdx]
                    g_mapCount = g_mapCount + 1
                }
                else
                    capacityWarning("confirmed mapping list", MAX_BSDS)
            }
            else
            {
                // No automatic match - leave it for the admin to map by hand.
                if (g_curACount < MAX_BSDS)
                {
                    g_curNameA[g_curACount] = namesA[i]
                    g_curFolderA[g_curACount] = foldersA[i]
                    g_curA[g_curACount] = formatEntry(foldersA[i], namesA[i])
                    g_curACount = g_curACount + 1
                }
                else
                    capacityWarning("Project A unmapped BSD list", MAX_BSDS)
            }
        }
    }

    if (namesBCount > 0)
    {
        for j in 0:namesBCount-1 do
        {
            if (!usedB[j])
            {
                if (g_curBCount < MAX_BSDS)
                {
                    g_curNameB[g_curBCount] = namesB[j]
                    g_curFolderB[g_curBCount] = foldersB[j]
                    g_curB[g_curBCount] = formatEntry(foldersB[j], namesB[j])
                    g_curBCount = g_curBCount + 1
                }
                else
                    capacityWarning("Project B unmapped BSD list", MAX_BSDS)
            }
        }
    }

    // ---- 3. build the initial display text for the mappings list ----

    string initialMapDisplay[500]   // size must match MAX_BSDS
    int initialMapDisplayCount = 0
    if (g_mapCount > 0)
    {
        for i in 0:g_mapCount-1 do
        {
            initialMapDisplay[initialMapDisplayCount] =
                formatEntry(g_mapFolderA[i], g_mapNameA[i]) " -> " formatEntry(g_mapFolderB[i], g_mapNameB[i])
            initialMapDisplayCount = initialMapDisplayCount + 1
        }
    }

    log("Baseline Set Definitions found (all folders, recursively) - Project A: " namesACount
        "   Project B: " namesBCount)
    log("Exact folder+name matches pre-mapped automatically: " g_mapCount)

    // ---- 4. build the dialog itself ----
    //
    // list() widgets are populated with insert() calls rather than by
    // relying on whatever happens to be in the backing array at creation
    // time - insert()/delete()/get() is the only list-content behaviour
    // confirmed from working examples, so we lean on that exclusively.
    // "placeholder" is just a throwaway 1-element array to satisfy each
    // list() call's parameter; the real content is added right after via
    // insert().

    string placeholder[1]

    g_mapDlg = create("Map Baseline Set Definitions")

    label(g_mapDlg, "Project A: " rootA)
    g_listA = list(g_mapDlg, "Unmapped Baseline Set Definitions in A (folder :: name)", 10, placeholder)
    if (g_curACount > 0)
        for i in 0:g_curACount-1 do
            insert(g_listA, i, g_curA[i])

    label(g_mapDlg, "Project B: " rootB)
    g_listB = list(g_mapDlg, "Unmapped Baseline Set Definitions in B (folder :: name)", 10, placeholder)
    if (g_curBCount > 0)
        for i in 0:g_curBCount-1 do
            insert(g_listB, i, g_curB[i])

    apply(g_mapDlg, "Map Selected Pair ->", cbAddMapping)
    apply(g_mapDlg, "Remove Selected Mapping", cbRemoveMapping)

    label(g_mapDlg, "Confirmed mappings (identical folder+name were pre-matched automatically):")
    g_listMap = list(g_mapDlg, "Confirmed mappings (A -> B)", 10, placeholder)
    if (initialMapDisplayCount > 0)
        for i in 0:initialMapDisplayCount-1 do
            insert(g_listMap, i, initialMapDisplay[i])

    g_status = field(g_mapDlg, "Status",
        "Select one BSD on each side, then click \"Map Selected Pair ->\". "
        "Anything left unmapped when you click \"Run Alignment\" will be "
        "created fresh on the other side, in the matching subfolder.", 70, false)

    ok(g_mapDlg, "Run Alignment", cbRunAlignment)
    ok(g_mapDlg, "Cancel", cbCancelMapping)
    close(g_mapDlg, false, cbCancelMapping)   // window's own close box = Cancel

    show(g_mapDlg)
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------
// MAIN
// ------------------------------------------------------------------

void main()
{
    openLog()

    log("================================================================")
    log("Baseline alignment run")
    log("  Project A: " PROJ_A_PATH)
    log("  Project B: " PROJ_B_PATH)
    log("  APPLY_CHANGES=" (APPLY_CHANGES ? "true" : "false")
        "  CREATE_MISSING_BASELINE_SETS=" (CREATE_MISSING_BASELINE_SETS ? "true" : "false"))
    log("================================================================")

    Folder projA = folder(PROJ_A_PATH)
    Folder projB = folder(PROJ_B_PATH)

    if (null projA)
    {
        log("ERROR: could not open project at \"" PROJ_A_PATH "\"")
        closeLog()
        return
    }
    if (null projB)
    {
        log("ERROR: could not open project at \"" PROJ_B_PATH "\"")
        closeLog()
        return
    }

    log("Total captured Baseline Sets right now (all folders, recursively) - Project A: "
        countCapturedBaselineSetsRecursive(projA) "   Project B: " countCapturedBaselineSetsRecursive(projB))

    if (APPLY_CHANGES)
    {
        if (!confirm("APPLY_CHANGES is ON.\n\nAfter you confirm the Baseline Set Definition "
                      "mapping in the next dialog, this script may create Baseline Set "
                      "Definitions, change their module membership, and (if enabled) capture "
                      "new Baseline Sets in:\n  " PROJ_A_PATH "\nand/or\n  " PROJ_B_PATH "\n\n"
                      "These actions are effectively permanent. Continue?"))
        {
            log("User cancelled before the mapping dialog was shown.")
            closeLog()
            return
        }
    }

    showMappingDialog(projA, PROJ_A_PATH, projB, PROJ_B_PATH)
    // Execution continues asynchronously from here: the rest of the
    // workflow happens inside cbRunAlignment / cbCancelMapping once the
    // user interacts with the dialog shown above.
}

main()
